1
00:00:02,509 --> 00:00:04,552
KATARA: Water.

2
00:00:04,636 --> 00:00:06,429
Earth.

3
00:00:06,554 --> 00:00:08,932
Fire.

4
00:00:09,015 --> 00:00:11,226
Air.

5
00:00:11,351 --> 00:00:15,063
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

6
00:00:15,188 --> 00:00:19,692
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

7
00:00:19,817 --> 00:00:23,321
Only the Avatar, master of
all four elements, could stop them.

8
00:00:23,446 --> 00:00:25,406
But when the world
needed him most,

9
00:00:25,532 --> 00:00:27,242
he vanished.

10
00:00:27,367 --> 00:00:30,995
A hundred years passed, and my brother
and I discovered the new Avatar,

11
00:00:31,120 --> 00:00:32,830
an airbender named Aang.

12
00:00:32,914 --> 00:00:35,041
And although his
airbending skills are great,

13
00:00:35,124 --> 00:00:37,752
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

14
00:00:37,835 --> 00:00:38,836
AANG: Oof.

15
00:00:38,920 --> 00:00:41,673
But I believe
Aang can save the world.

16
00:00:48,012 --> 00:00:50,265
MAN: Previously on Avatar...

17
00:00:50,348 --> 00:00:53,101
I came along because I wanted to make sure
you got through

18
00:00:53,184 --> 00:00:54,477
the Serpent's Pass safely.

19
00:00:54,561 --> 00:00:57,355
But now I need to get back
to the other Kyoshi Warriors.

20
00:00:57,480 --> 00:00:59,566
You stole Appa.

21
00:00:59,649 --> 00:01:01,401
Where is he,
what did you do to him?

22
00:01:01,484 --> 00:01:02,986
I traded him.

23
00:01:03,111 --> 00:01:05,530
He's probably in
Ba Sing Se by now.

24
00:01:05,655 --> 00:01:08,157
AANG: He's here, I can feel it.

25
00:01:08,283 --> 00:01:10,827
I am Long Feng,
head of the Dai Li.

26
00:01:10,952 --> 00:01:13,204
I understand you've been looking for
your bison,

27
00:01:13,288 --> 00:01:17,584
it would be quite a shame if you were
not able to complete your quest.

28
00:01:24,591 --> 00:01:26,551
APPA: ( RUMBLING )

29
00:01:30,722 --> 00:01:32,724
No, stop sinking!

30
00:01:32,849 --> 00:01:35,268
( GROWLING )

31
00:01:38,438 --> 00:01:39,522
( GRUNTING )

32
00:01:39,606 --> 00:01:41,065
Whoa!
Augh.

33
00:01:41,190 --> 00:01:42,191
( SCREAMING )

34
00:01:42,692 --> 00:01:46,237
( ROARING )

35
00:01:47,488 --> 00:01:49,782
Don't make me put this down!

36
00:01:53,578 --> 00:01:55,622
MAN: Put a muzzle on it!

37
00:01:58,833 --> 00:02:00,460
Augh, oof!

38
00:02:02,045 --> 00:02:03,504
Augh!

39
00:02:14,974 --> 00:02:17,185
( ROARING )

40
00:02:17,310 --> 00:02:19,270
MEN: ( GRUNTING )

41
00:02:31,532 --> 00:02:34,160
I'm sorry, Appa.

42
00:02:39,248 --> 00:02:41,376
APPA: ( RUMBLING )

43
00:02:54,972 --> 00:02:56,140
MAN: Ransack his saddle.

44
00:02:56,224 --> 00:02:58,476
Who knows what treasures
are stashed in there?

45
00:02:59,644 --> 00:03:01,020
( ROARING )

46
00:03:01,145 --> 00:03:03,481
He's tied up good,
he can't hurt you.

47
00:03:04,774 --> 00:03:06,651
( SNIFFING )

48
00:03:06,776 --> 00:03:07,777
( SNEEZING )

49
00:03:13,157 --> 00:03:16,828
What's your father gonna do when he
finds out we lost a sandsailer?

50
00:03:16,953 --> 00:03:18,037
Nothing.

51
00:03:18,162 --> 00:03:20,456
It's the one we stole
from the Hammi Tribe.

52
00:03:20,581 --> 00:03:21,958
Did you empty the saddle?

53
00:03:23,459 --> 00:03:24,836
That's it?

54
00:03:24,961 --> 00:03:25,962
Nothing but garbage!

55
00:03:26,587 --> 00:03:29,549
Ah, doesn't matter.

56
00:03:29,674 --> 00:03:33,261
We'll still make a profit from selling him
to those beetle-headed merchants.

57
00:03:43,396 --> 00:03:46,524
( RUMBLING )

58
00:03:47,775 --> 00:03:48,860
How's his temper?

59
00:03:48,943 --> 00:03:50,653
Uh, pretty good.

60
00:03:50,778 --> 00:03:52,530
( ROARING )

61
00:03:53,656 --> 00:03:55,450
( LAUGHING NERVOUSLY )
Most of the time.

62
00:03:56,033 --> 00:03:59,287
I bet someone will pay
a fortune for him in Ba Sing Se.

63
00:03:59,412 --> 00:04:02,039
All right, you've got a deal.

64
00:04:13,760 --> 00:04:15,762
AANG: Appa!

65
00:04:15,887 --> 00:04:17,221
Appa!

66
00:04:20,349 --> 00:04:23,019
( GRUNTING )

67
00:04:27,023 --> 00:04:29,066
He's your problem now!
( LAUGHING )

68
00:04:30,234 --> 00:04:31,611
What?

69
00:04:36,157 --> 00:04:38,075
MAN: Whoa!

70
00:04:38,201 --> 00:04:40,912
We need the shirshu spit darts!

71
00:04:41,037 --> 00:04:42,163
Got 'em.

72
00:04:42,246 --> 00:04:43,623
O.K., big fella,

73
00:04:43,748 --> 00:04:46,125
You're gonna take
a nice, little snoozle.

74
00:04:55,760 --> 00:04:58,221
( SHOUTING ) Appa!

75
00:05:00,473 --> 00:05:02,517
No.

76
00:05:03,601 --> 00:05:05,478
( SHOUTING ) No!

77
00:05:10,024 --> 00:05:12,860
( RUMBLING )

78
00:05:12,985 --> 00:05:15,112
We've gotta get rid of this one.

79
00:05:15,196 --> 00:05:17,114
He's too much trouble.

80
00:05:17,240 --> 00:05:18,783
We could sell him for parts.

81
00:05:18,908 --> 00:05:22,328
( RUMBLING )

82
00:05:22,411 --> 00:05:27,458
Oh, I understand you've had
a rather hard time, lately.

83
00:05:27,542 --> 00:05:29,877
That's too bad.

84
00:05:29,961 --> 00:05:35,383
You probably felt you had no choice
but to behave outrageously.

85
00:05:35,466 --> 00:05:36,717
Like a wild animal.

86
00:05:37,802 --> 00:05:40,263
But don't worry,
you won't anymore.

87
00:05:40,972 --> 00:05:43,391
Because I am going to break you.

88
00:05:46,394 --> 00:05:47,770
APPA: ( RUMBLING )

89
00:05:53,609 --> 00:05:55,778
( RUMBLING )

90
00:06:00,283 --> 00:06:01,951
( SQUAWKING )

91
00:06:03,160 --> 00:06:04,954
Hungry?

92
00:06:05,079 --> 00:06:07,832
Don't worry,
I'm going to feed you too.

93
00:06:08,541 --> 00:06:10,501
But not yet.

94
00:06:11,043 --> 00:06:14,630
First I'm going to show you
how you'll earn it.

95
00:06:18,217 --> 00:06:19,635
( SQUAWKING )

96
00:06:22,054 --> 00:06:23,222
( SQUAWKING )

97
00:06:39,530 --> 00:06:43,576
Of course, when you perform,
the hoops will be flaming.

98
00:06:43,743 --> 00:06:47,538
And if you are careful,
you won't get burned.

99
00:06:48,205 --> 00:06:50,166
( BURPING )

100
00:06:50,291 --> 00:06:52,752
You're about to be sorry.

101
00:06:54,962 --> 00:06:57,214
( ROARING )

102
00:06:57,340 --> 00:07:00,468
It's obvious that whoever
your previous owner was,

103
00:07:00,593 --> 00:07:05,765
he had no idea
how to handle you properly.

104
00:07:05,890 --> 00:07:07,767
( CIRCUS MUSIC PLAYING )

105
00:07:18,110 --> 00:07:19,987
I'm gonna go get
a bag of sizzle-crisps.

106
00:07:20,071 --> 00:07:22,031
Stay here and stay away
from that monster!

107
00:07:22,490 --> 00:07:25,660
Behave yourself
or you'll regret it.

108
00:07:27,453 --> 00:07:31,958
( RUMBLING )

109
00:07:40,174 --> 00:07:43,135
He's a difficult creature,
stubborn and willful.

110
00:07:43,219 --> 00:07:45,137
I need more time with him.

111
00:07:45,221 --> 00:07:46,514
It's too risky right now.

112
00:07:46,597 --> 00:07:47,974
Too risky?

113
00:07:48,057 --> 00:07:49,684
What're you talking about?

114
00:07:49,767 --> 00:07:52,353
This is the circus,
home of fear and danger!

115
00:07:52,436 --> 00:07:55,147
I want the wind buffalo
to perform tonight.

116
00:07:56,315 --> 00:07:58,943
If you don't behave yourself...

117
00:07:59,402 --> 00:08:00,611
You'll regret it.

118
00:08:00,736 --> 00:08:01,821
( ROARING )

119
00:08:10,454 --> 00:08:11,998
Let's go!

120
00:08:12,081 --> 00:08:13,082
See you later, buddy.

121
00:08:20,965 --> 00:08:25,094
( APPLAUSE AND CHEERING )

122
00:08:25,177 --> 00:08:29,223
MAN: Ladies and gentlemen,
now for something truly special.

123
00:08:30,933 --> 00:08:34,353
A noble beast
so magnificent and rare,

124
00:08:34,437 --> 00:08:38,107
it hasn't been seen
by human eyes in generations.

125
00:08:38,190 --> 00:08:39,483
I give you...

126
00:08:39,567 --> 00:08:42,403
The wind buffalo!

127
00:08:45,448 --> 00:08:47,992
( LAUGHTER )

128
00:08:50,161 --> 00:08:52,329
Up.

129
00:08:52,455 --> 00:08:53,622
( LAUGHTER )

130
00:08:53,748 --> 00:08:56,208
Up, you insolent cow!

131
00:08:57,376 --> 00:08:59,336
( ROARING )

132
00:08:59,462 --> 00:09:02,465
Run away, get away from him!

133
00:09:05,760 --> 00:09:07,762
AUDIENCE: Whoa,
amazing, fabulous!

134
00:09:19,106 --> 00:09:20,149
Augh!

135
00:09:20,232 --> 00:09:21,233
Ugh.

136
00:09:21,942 --> 00:09:27,031
( LAUGHTER )

137
00:09:28,365 --> 00:09:30,868
( ROARING )

138
00:09:31,494 --> 00:09:32,495
Go.

139
00:09:32,578 --> 00:09:33,579
You can do it.

140
00:09:38,375 --> 00:09:40,127
Get back here, you stupid beast!

141
00:09:47,259 --> 00:09:48,594
AUDIENCE: Oh...

142
00:10:11,200 --> 00:10:13,536
( GROANING )

143
00:10:30,594 --> 00:10:34,557
( ROARING )

144
00:10:37,226 --> 00:10:39,854
( SNIFFING )

145
00:10:52,283 --> 00:10:55,619
( BUZZING )

146
00:11:10,968 --> 00:11:14,054
( GROANING )

147
00:11:38,996 --> 00:11:43,250
( PURRING )

148
00:11:53,344 --> 00:11:55,512
WOMAN: Choose well.

149
00:11:55,679 --> 00:11:58,432
A sky bison is
a companion for life.

150
00:12:10,444 --> 00:12:12,947
( GRUNTING )

151
00:12:13,072 --> 00:12:16,242
I guess this means
we'll always be together.

152
00:12:16,367 --> 00:12:19,370
( LAUGHING )

153
00:12:22,331 --> 00:12:24,667
Always.

154
00:12:27,002 --> 00:12:30,089
MAN: ( SCREAMING )
It's some kind of monster!

155
00:12:31,674 --> 00:12:36,345
( GROWLING )

156
00:12:36,470 --> 00:12:38,013
( ROARING )

157
00:12:41,141 --> 00:12:43,394
( SCREAMING )

158
00:12:43,519 --> 00:12:44,853
( ROARING )

159
00:12:55,698 --> 00:12:57,449
( GASPING )

160
00:12:57,574 --> 00:13:00,536
Uncle, what are you looking at?

161
00:13:00,661 --> 00:13:02,121
Is there something out there?

162
00:13:02,246 --> 00:13:04,373
Muh, it's nothing.

163
00:13:04,498 --> 00:13:07,251
Go back to sleep.

164
00:13:07,376 --> 00:13:08,502
( SIGHING )

165
00:13:24,893 --> 00:13:27,021
( DISTANT SQUEALING )

166
00:13:27,146 --> 00:13:29,732
( ROARING )

167
00:13:36,989 --> 00:13:38,282
( ROARING/SQUEALING )

168
00:13:38,407 --> 00:13:41,618
( ROARING )

169
00:13:47,291 --> 00:13:49,168
( ROARING/SQUEALING )

170
00:13:56,842 --> 00:13:58,344
( ROARING/SQUEALING )

171
00:13:59,428 --> 00:14:00,596
( ROARING )

172
00:14:09,063 --> 00:14:10,814
( SQUEALING )

173
00:14:15,444 --> 00:14:17,613
( ROARING )

174
00:14:38,342 --> 00:14:41,470
( BIRDS CHIRPING )

175
00:14:47,976 --> 00:14:49,228
Must've been some fight.

176
00:14:49,353 --> 00:14:52,439
Wait, let me see that.

177
00:14:52,564 --> 00:14:54,858
No, it couldn't be.

178
00:14:59,988 --> 00:15:01,949
( GASPING )
Appa?

179
00:15:02,074 --> 00:15:03,909
Oh, no.

180
00:15:04,034 --> 00:15:05,035
( GROWLING )

181
00:15:11,500 --> 00:15:14,211
It's gonna be O.K., Appa.

182
00:15:14,336 --> 00:15:18,715
I have to leave, but I'm gonna
be back soon with help.

183
00:15:22,302 --> 00:15:23,679
No sudden movements.

184
00:15:23,887 --> 00:15:26,640
He's been lost for a while,
and he looks like he's hurt.

185
00:15:26,765 --> 00:15:29,017
He's shy around people
and scared.

186
00:15:29,143 --> 00:15:31,437
Stay low and stay quiet.

187
00:15:31,603 --> 00:15:34,356
I can't believe
you found the Avatar's bison.

188
00:15:34,481 --> 00:15:36,692
Didn't you just see
the Avatar a few days go?

189
00:15:36,775 --> 00:15:39,987
Yes, so he can't be
too far from here.

190
00:15:40,112 --> 00:15:43,073
It's our responsibility
to get Appa back to him safely.

191
00:15:43,198 --> 00:15:45,784
This could be our most important
mission yet.

192
00:15:48,245 --> 00:15:49,329
( GROWLING )

193
00:15:49,455 --> 00:15:52,207
Give him some space!

194
00:15:54,418 --> 00:15:58,422
Appa, it's me, Suki.

195
00:15:58,547 --> 00:16:01,592
I'm a friend.

196
00:16:01,717 --> 00:16:04,011
( RUMBLING )

197
00:16:04,136 --> 00:16:05,137
I want to help you.

198
00:16:05,220 --> 00:16:07,431
You're hurt.

199
00:16:07,556 --> 00:16:09,308
We can help you feel better.

200
00:16:09,433 --> 00:16:10,559
( RUMBLING )

201
00:16:10,684 --> 00:16:14,146
And we can help you find Aang.

202
00:16:31,288 --> 00:16:32,873
( ROARING )

203
00:16:36,335 --> 00:16:38,128
My, my, you're easy to find.

204
00:16:38,253 --> 00:16:42,508
It's really astounding my brother hasn't
captured you yet.

205
00:16:42,633 --> 00:16:45,469
( GROWLING )

206
00:16:51,475 --> 00:16:52,476
( GROWLING )

207
00:16:54,937 --> 00:16:56,480
What do you want with us?

208
00:16:56,605 --> 00:17:00,943
Who are you,
the Avatar's fan girls?

209
00:17:01,068 --> 00:17:03,320
Oh, I get it!

210
00:17:03,445 --> 00:17:04,738
Good one, Azula.

211
00:17:04,863 --> 00:17:07,741
If you're looking for
the Avatar, you're out of luck.

212
00:17:07,866 --> 00:17:10,827
AZULA: ( SIGHING )
I knew this was a waste of time.

213
00:17:10,953 --> 00:17:11,995
No Avatar, huh?

214
00:17:12,120 --> 00:17:13,580
Well, that's O.K.

215
00:17:13,705 --> 00:17:15,457
Any friend of the Avatar...

216
00:17:15,582 --> 00:17:17,501
Is an enemy of mine!

217
00:17:23,757 --> 00:17:25,717
Augh!
Uh, huh?

218
00:17:25,842 --> 00:17:28,971
You're so colorful,
it's making me nauseous.

219
00:17:34,309 --> 00:17:35,936
Ugh, ugh, ugh!

220
00:17:36,061 --> 00:17:37,604
You're not prettier than we are.

221
00:17:43,443 --> 00:17:44,444
( GROWLING )

222
00:17:45,153 --> 00:17:46,780
Afraid of fire, I see?

223
00:17:46,947 --> 00:17:48,657
That's good, you should be.

224
00:17:49,116 --> 00:17:51,994
Go, Appa!
Fly away from here!

225
00:17:58,792 --> 00:18:00,252
( GRUNTING )

226
00:18:00,377 --> 00:18:02,504
( GROWLING )

227
00:18:09,886 --> 00:18:11,054
Get out of here!

228
00:18:11,179 --> 00:18:12,764
You have to find Aang!

229
00:18:12,889 --> 00:18:13,890
We'll be O.K.

230
00:18:23,400 --> 00:18:26,361
Don't you know
fans just make flames stronger?

231
00:18:31,408 --> 00:18:32,409
( RUMBLING )

232
00:19:00,228 --> 00:19:02,397
( PURRING )

233
00:19:08,945 --> 00:19:14,493
( PURRING )

234
00:19:16,453 --> 00:19:17,871
( COUGHING )

235
00:19:25,337 --> 00:19:27,172
( GASPING )

236
00:19:31,968 --> 00:19:34,096
Hello.

237
00:19:34,221 --> 00:19:35,722
I am Guru Pathik.

238
00:19:35,847 --> 00:19:37,182
( RUMBLING CONFUSEDLY )

239
00:19:42,604 --> 00:19:45,816
I know I'm not
the person you expected.

240
00:19:45,941 --> 00:19:49,736
And I didn't expect to be licked by
a giant tongue just now.

241
00:19:49,861 --> 00:19:51,863
( SIGHING )
the world is full of surprises.

242
00:19:51,988 --> 00:19:55,283
( GROWLING )

243
00:20:01,832 --> 00:20:03,875
( GROWLING )

244
00:20:28,567 --> 00:20:29,568
Oh, dear.

245
00:20:29,860 --> 00:20:33,447
You've been through
so much, recently.

246
00:20:33,572 --> 00:20:35,115
Hurt and betrayed.

247
00:20:35,240 --> 00:20:37,075
So twisted-up inside.

248
00:20:41,204 --> 00:20:42,789
You're still full of love.

249
00:20:42,914 --> 00:20:46,835
( SIGHING ) but fear has moved in
where trust should be.

250
00:20:46,960 --> 00:20:51,923
I've been expecting you and
the young Avatar for quite a long time.

251
00:20:52,048 --> 00:20:56,094
I had a vision many years ago
of helping him.

252
00:20:56,219 --> 00:20:59,347
That's why I came to
the Eastern Air Temple.

253
00:21:04,019 --> 00:21:07,606
Oh, your emotions
are so turbulent.

254
00:21:07,731 --> 00:21:10,859
Like swirling storm clouds.

255
00:21:12,527 --> 00:21:16,239
Let the clouds in your mind
be gentle, peaceful ones.

256
00:21:35,592 --> 00:21:37,969
Someone looks very well-rested,

257
00:21:38,094 --> 00:21:40,639
judging by your bed head.

258
00:21:40,764 --> 00:21:41,765
( ROARING )

259
00:22:04,830 --> 00:22:07,457
I have prepared
a message for Aang.

260
00:22:07,624 --> 00:22:09,584
May I attach it to your horn?

261
00:22:09,709 --> 00:22:12,337
( RUMBLING )

262
00:22:15,382 --> 00:22:18,760
You and the Avatar's
energies are mixed.

263
00:22:18,885 --> 00:22:21,596
You have an unbreakable bond.

264
00:22:21,721 --> 00:22:26,601
By reading your energy,
I can sense where Aang is.

265
00:22:28,979 --> 00:22:32,566
Funny, what invisible strings
connect us all.

266
00:22:42,033 --> 00:22:45,370
I'll see you again, great beast.

267
00:22:47,831 --> 00:22:50,208
( RUMBLING )

